{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789209151,"nonce":"7Tg91tFI1W3bCoHhwPlTHoVkoEw=","title":"translate_air_v2 cannot take a widened function; only the OSR body materialises pending ints and lane-typed slots","message":"crates/ash/src/llvm/function/mod.rs (build_air_osr_body prelude) materialises air.pending_ints as Int_{idx} globals and re-types every value with lanes \u003e= 2 to a \u003cN x T\u003e slot. translate_air_v2 (air_emit.rs) does neither, and the comment on emit_air_vector claiming it does is wrong (so was 828c746 #0). On the ordinary path a widened function fails 'AIR Int names no constant' in ensure_int_global (module.rs), VecSplat fails 'destination is not a vector', and VecLoad/VecBinOp into scalar slots compute lane 0 only. Latent today because lanes_fit refuses most shapes, but the O3 pipeline runs Widen last and --build lowers every function through compile_function. Fix: one AIR-aware register allocation shared by both entry points (values, cells, lanes, pending ints), replacing allocate_registers(\u0026lowering) for AIR.","files":null}]}